{"app":"spr-flow","version":3,"nodes":[{"id":"note","type":"info","position":{"x":-806,"y":-496},"data":{"title":"SPR by grating coupling, conical incidence","text":"Gold grating (Λ = 500 nm, 10 nm deep, fill 0.5) on gold, 633 nm, TM light from air, the plane of incidence turned by the azimuth φ from the grating vector (Compute RCWA: φ port, here a Sweep 0 / 15 / 30 / 45°).\n\nThe order −1 excites the plasmon when |k∥ − K x̂| = n_sp, n_sp = Re √(ε_Au/(ε_Au + 1)): sin θ = (λ/Λ) cos φ − √(n_sp² − (λ/Λ)² sin² φ) → 12.8° / 13.3° / 15.4° / 20.9° for φ = 0 / 15 / 30 / 45° (a shallow grating; this 10 nm one shifts the dips by ≈ −0.2° to −0.4°). Min / max finds the dip of each φ. At φ ≠ 0 TE and TM are coupled: the second plot shows the TM light reflected as TE (R into TE), zero at φ = 0. The RCWA field map (press Run) shows the plasmon at the dip of φ = 30°, with all six field components (conical incidence).\n\nValidation: conical RCWA = RETICOLO (res1 with delta0) on 19 cases, efficiencies and their TE / TM parts to 1e-11.","color":"#8a93a6","width":380,"height":300}},{"id":"air","type":"material","position":{"x":-806,"y":-47},"data":{"materialId":"Air","color":"#f4f6fa","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"au","type":"material","position":{"x":-806,"y":201},"data":{"materialId":"Au","color":"#e0b43c","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"gr","type":"grating","position":{"x":-390,"y":-47},"data":{"label":"Au grating","profile":"lamellar","period":500,"thickness":10,"fill":0.5,"fillTop":0.3,"shift":0.5,"slices":10,"nx":32,"pixels":[],"materials":2}},{"id":"stack","type":"combine","position":{"x":78,"y":71},"data":{"name":"Grating on gold","count":1}},{"id":"wl","type":"param","position":{"x":78,"y":-236},"data":{"quantity":"lambda","mode":"constant","value":633,"min":500,"max":900,"step":1}},{"id":"th","type":"param","position":{"x":78,"y":389},"data":{"quantity":"theta","mode":"range","value":20,"min":8,"max":26,"step":0.05}},{"id"